escription\": \"Dylan Castillo's deep-dive investigation into whether AI labs have been deliberately training models to draw pelicans riding bicycles. Testing 8 animals \\u00d7 6 vehicles = 48 prompts across 7 different models (GPT-5.6 Terra, Claude Sonnet 5, Gemini 3.5 Flash, Grok 4.5, Qwen3.7-Max, GLM-5.2, and DeepSeek V4 Pro). Conclusion: No evidence found of pelimaxxing - pelicans aren't drawn better than other animals, and labs don't show special capability at this specific combination.\",\n    40→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison (citing Dylan Castillo)\",\n    41→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    42→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net\",\n    43→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-22\",\n    44→    \"topics\": [\n    45→      \"AI-evals\",\n    46→      \"model-testing\",\n    47→      \"benchmarking\",\n    48→      \"AI-behavior\",\n    49→      \"visual-models\"\n    50→    ],\n    51→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    52→  },\n    53→  {\n    54→    \"title\": \"Nativ: Run AI models locally on your Mac\",\n    55→    \"description\": \"Prince Canuma's new macOS desktop application that wraps MLX for running AI models locally on Mac. Similar to LM Studio, providing both a chat interface and a localhost API server. The app automatically picks up MLX models from the Hugging Face cache directory.\",\n    56→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    57→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    58→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net\",\n    59→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-21\",\n    60→    \"topics\": [\n    61→      \"local-LLMs\",\n    62→      \"MLX\",\n    63→      \"macOS\",\n    64→      \"AI-tools\",\n    65→      \"vision-LLMs\"\n    66→    ],\n    67→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    68→  },\n    69→  {\n    70→    \"title\": \"A Fireside Chat with Cat and Thariq from the Claude Code team\",\n    71→    \"description\": \"Discussion at AI Engineer World's Fair with Cat Wu and Thariq Shihipar from Anthropic's Claude Code team. Covered Claude Code, Claude Tag,