 reverse-engineer and automate devices in their homes\",\n   108→    \"description\": \"Insight on how coding agents are changing the economics of automation. Previously, reverse-engineering home devices had questionable ROI due to effort and maintenance concerns. AI agents dramatically reduce both the cost of initial implementation and the psychological burden of maintenance, enabling new types of personal automation projects.\",\n   109→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   110→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   111→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net\",\n   112→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-20\",\n   113→    \"topics\": [\n   114→      \"coding-agents\",\n   115→      \"AI-assisted-programming\",\n   116→      \"automation\",\n   117→      \"reverse-engineering\",\n   118→      \"developer-productivity\"\n   119→    ],\n   120→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n   121→  },\n   122→  {\n   123→    \"title\": \"Who's Afraid of Chinese Models?\",\n   124→    \"description\": \"Ben Thompson's proposal addressing hypocrisy of labs outlawing distillation while training on unlicensed data. Suggests US law making explicit that collecting data for training is fair use, and barring terms of service that forbid distillation. Discusses Alibaba's Qwen 3.8 Max release as open weights (2.4T parameters), potentially influenced by Xi Jinping's speech on open source collaboration.\",\n   125→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison (citing Ben Thompson)\",\n   126→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   127→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net\",\n   128→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-20\",\n   129→    \"topics\": [\n   130→      \"AI-in-China\",\n   131→      \"Qwen\",\n   132→      \"open-weights\",\n   133→      \"distillation\",\n   134→      \"AI-policy\",\n   135→      \"fair-use\",\n   136→      \"Alibaba\"\n   137→    ],\n   138→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n   139→  },\n   140→  {\n   141→    \"title\": \"Rewriting Bun in Rust - Claude Code now uses Rust port of Bun\",\n   142→    \"description\": \"Claude Code v2.1.181 and later use the Rust port of Bun. Investigation reveals Claude is running Bun v1.4.0 (not yet officially released, only in canary). Strings analysis shows 563 Rust source files embedded in the Claude binary, confirming the Rust version is in production across millions of devices.\",\n   143→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison (citing Jarred Sumner)\",\n   144→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   145→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net\",\n   146→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-19\",\n   147→    \"topics\": [\n   148→      \"Bun\",\n   149→      \"Rust\",\n   150→      \"Claude-Code\",\n   151→      \"JavaScript-runtime\",\n   152→      \"performance\"\n   153→    ],\n   154→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   155→  },\n   156→  {\n   157→    \"title\": \"AI Mania Is Eviscerating Global Decision-Making\",\n   158→    \"description\": \"Nik Suresh's perspective on AI mania overwhelming large companies. Anecdotes include an executive confessing they never used ChatGPT after producing a $2B+ revenue AI strategy, and engineers running Go-to-Zig rewrites just to appear productive on token leaderboards. Discusses how vendors can't challenge unrealistic 100x productivity claims without risking enterprise contracts.\",\n   159→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison (citing Nik Suresh)\",\n   160→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   161→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net\",\n   162→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-19\",\n   163→    \"topics\": [\n   164→      \"AI-ethics\",\n   165→      \"AI-hype\",\n   166→      \"enterprise-AI\",\n   167→      \"productivity\",\n   168→      \"AI-misuse\"\n   169→    ],\n   170→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n   171→  },\n   172→  {\n   173→    \"title\": \"Claude make Fable 5 permanent\",\n   174→    \"description\": \"Anthropic announced Fable 5 will be included in all Max and Team Premium plans at 50% of limits starting July 20. Pro and Team Standard users get access via usage credits with a one-time $100 credit. This 